## Installation

Prerequisites:
- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/).
{%- if agent_providers.size > 1 %}
- For the model-backed capabilities, one of:
{%- elsif agent_providers.size == 1 %}
- For the model-backed capabilities:
{%- endif %}
{% if agent_providers contains "copilot" %}  - `copilot` agent provider: [GitHub CLI](https://cli.github.com/) signed in to an account with a [GitHub Copilot subscription](https://github.com/github/copilot-cli#prerequisites).
{% endif %}{% if agent_providers contains "amplifier-agent" %}  - `amplifier-agent` agent provider: the model provider's credentials, for instance `OPENAI_API_KEY` for the default `openai/...` models. See [providers](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-agent/blob/v0.22.0/docs/providers.md).
{% endif %}{% if agent_providers contains "codex" %}  - `codex` agent provider: the [Codex CLI](https://github.com/openai/codex) signed in with ChatGPT or an API key. See [authentication](https://developers.openai.com/codex/auth).
{% endif %}{% if agent_providers contains "claude" %}  - `claude` agent provider: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, or any of its other supported modes of [authentication](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/quickstart).
{% endif %}
```bash
{% if agent_providers.size > 1 %}# Install the tool, choosing the provider(s) you want
{% endif %}uv tool install {{ tool_source }}
```

To use it as a library:

```bash
uv add {{ library_source }}
```

To run it once without installing:

```bash
uvx --from {{ run_source }} {{ name }} --help
```
{% if skill %}
To teach a coding agent how to use it, install the [skill](skills/{{ name }}/SKILL.md):

```bash
npx skills add {{ skill_source }}
```
{% endif %}
To update:

```bash
uv tool upgrade {{ name }}
{% if skill %}npx skills update {{ name }}   # add --global if the skill was installed globally
{% endif %}```

To uninstall:

```bash
uv tool uninstall {{ name }}
{% if skill %}npx skills remove {{ name }}   # add --global if the skill was installed globally
{% endif %}```

Verify an install with `{{ name }} manifest`, which needs no credentials.

